#!/usr/bin/python3 -I
"""evals: self-evals. Replays real owner requests (a private corpus) against my setup (CLAUDE.md, FACTS.md, skills,
agents, hooks, memory) in a sandbox and scores the behaviour, so a change to me is measured before it is trusted.

  evals run [--case GLOB]... [--tag T]... [--area A]... [--changed [--since REV]] [--rev REV] [-j N] [--runs N]
            [--max-cases 60] [--budget-min 30] [--case-timeout S] [--case-usd X] [--model M] [--effort E]
            [--judge-model M] [--no-judge] [--keep] [--label L] [--threshold F] [--json] [--cron] [--dry-run]
  evals compare REV_A REV_B [same filters]  score two brain revisions on the same cases (results cached per setup hash)
  evals report [RUN|last] [--json] [--failures]
  evals list [--tag T] [--json]             the corpus: id, area, tags, graders
  evals history [-n N] [--json]
  evals summary [--hours 26] [--json]       latest run vs the previous comparable run (self-review reads this)
  evals isolation [--live]                  prove the sandbox: user, env whitelist, network guard, file permissions
  evals gc [--days 7]                       remove old sandboxes (results are kept)
  evals setup [--check]                     build / check the Inspect venv from inspect-requirements.txt (pinned)
  evals inspect ARGS..                      the venv's `inspect` CLI (view / log list default to the private log dir)

Runner: Inspect AI (the corpus as a dataset, the evalbot worker as the solver, graders + gates + the judge rubric as
the scorer, the judge through the `claudecode` provider = `claude -p` as the eval user). `evals` re-executes itself
under the venv; no venv -> run/compare stop with "run `evals setup`". report|history|summary also read result.json / history rows
without a runner field. --changed --paths P.. selects cases for
given paths (HOME-relative, or ~/opt/assistant sources mapped through its deploy manifest) instead of the brain diff.

A case runs in a fresh sandbox HOME (~/jobs/evals/runs/RUN/CASE/home): the setup under test (live files, or brain REV
via git archive), the case fixtures, a recording stub for every ~/bin script and fake MCP servers with the production
names (Telegram, Calendar), plus the MCP server `hub` (--hub on, the default: the deployed typed tools in a world-
readable venv copy, HOME = the sandbox, so every CLI it wraps is a stub). `claude -p` (stream-json, same model/effort as the main session) runs there as the
unprivileged user evalbot (no sudo/cron; can't read 0600/0700 secrets or write the real home) with a rebuilt
environment, the LD_PRELOAD network guard (no loopback, LAN or Telegram; the model API stays reachable) and an eval
hook that maps real-home paths to their twin in the sandbox home. The model access token reaches the worker on stdin, never argv or disk.
Scoring: deterministic graders (plugin-eval vocabulary: stub / tool / mcp calls with input regex and min/max, reply
count, lines and regex, trace regex, tool-result regex (result_re / no_result_re, `on` = tool-name regex), order,
files), then ONE LLM-judge call per case for its soft criteria; the judge also sees the context per-message hooks added. Case score
= weighted share of graders passed; pass = 1.0. Gates (run finished, no blocked network attempt, no secret in what was
sent) zero the score when they fail; critical graders mark privacy/safety failures. A run that ended in an API error
(usage limit, 429, 529 overloaded, 5xx; or its judge call did) is infra, not behaviour: status "error", no score, not
judged, left out of the case, run and history scores (and so of `summary` and the reflex review); reports count it
apart, and a run where every case errored is "no data" (score None), never 0 (last-rev then stays).
Files: corpus ~/opt/evals-private (private), state ~/.local/state/evals (runs/RUN/result.json, history.jsonl, last-rev),
reports ~/reports/evals/RUN.md. Env: EVALS_CORPUS, EVALS_STATE, EVALS_JOBS, EVALS_REPORTS, EVALS_USER, EVALS_CLAUDE,
BRAIN_GIT_DIR, EVALS_NO_SUDO (tests: run workers as the caller), USAGE=off, EVALS_VENV, EVALS_LOGDIR
(Inspect logs, 0700), EVALS_LIB, EVALS_SHARE. Tests: ~/opt/evals-tests/run.sh.
"""
import argparse
import datetime as dt
import fnmatch
import glob
import hashlib
import io
import json
import os
import re
import shutil
import subprocess
import sys
import tarfile
import threading
